    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote 34 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. The suite passes with `python -m pytest -q tests`. The implementation validates `start`, `n` and every holiday and raises `TypeError` for the cases the spec lists. It then walks day by day in the requested direction, counting Monday-to-Friday days that are not holidays. For `n == 0` it moves forward to the next business day if `start` is not one. One test failed on my first run because I had the wrong expected date; I corrected the test, not the code. I could not measure line coverage, since the only shell command allowed is the test command. Every line and branch of `solution.py` is exercised by the tests, so I expect the 90% gate to pass, but that is unconfirmed.",
